Subject: [PATCH] Exit startup clock waits when the ROS context shuts down

Applies to ros-controls/mujoco_ros2_control tag 0.1.2

Stopping while the control thread waits for its first simulated clock tick
can invalidate the ROS context before the following sleep_for call. The
uncaught runtime_error terminates the process with SIGABRT

Use the controller manager's context for both waits, leave when startup
was interrupted, and suppress runtime_error only after that context has
actually shut down. Rethrow every runtime_error while the context remains
valid, preserving the existing behavior for genuine startup faults

diff --git a/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_ros2_control_node.cpp b/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_ros2_control_node.cpp
--- a/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_ros2_control_node.cpp
+++ b/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_ros2_control_node.cpp
@@ -140,8 +140,23 @@ int main(int argc, char ** argv)
       //
       // TODO: Potentially remove this node depending on what comes out of the upstream PR:
       // https://github.com/ros-controls/ros2_control/pull/2654
-      cm->get_clock()->wait_until_started();
-      cm->get_clock()->sleep_for(rclcpp::Duration::from_seconds(1.0 / cm->get_update_rate()));
+      const auto context = cm->get_node_base_interface()->get_context();
+      try
+      {
+        if (!cm->get_clock()->wait_until_started(context))
+        {
+          return;
+        }
+        cm->get_clock()->sleep_for(rclcpp::Duration::from_seconds(1.0 / cm->get_update_rate()), context);
+      }
+      catch (const std::runtime_error &)
+      {
+        if (context->is_valid())
+        {
+          throw;
+        }
+        return;
+      }
 
       // for calculating sleep time
       auto const period = std::chrono::nanoseconds(1'000'000'000 / cm->get_update_rate());
